Presence of this file makes build.cmd compile raycast.pas with -O2, into its
own unit directory rather than the shared one.

The optimisation itself is worth about +7% on the cast and +4% on the frame,
measured on hardware. It was declined for a long time for a good reason: FPC
puts compiled units wherever -FU points, build/ is ONE directory shared by
every target, and so optimised vga/cpu/net .ppu files would be what UGET,
UPUT and TFTP linked next. Those are the programs the box needs in order to
be reachable at all; they are I/O bound, so there is nothing there to win,
and a miscompile in one of them is the failure this project designs against.

Pointing this target at its own -FU directory removes the coupling rather
than the gain. Nothing else in starter/ is affected, and deleting this file
puts raycast back on the shared unoptimised units.
